SQLite database backend (Core3.DBType = "sqlite", Core3.DBPath): a single-file database
created with its schema and galaxy row on first start, so one-PC installs need no MySQL/MariaDB.
SqliteDialect lets Core3's MySQL-flavoured SQL run unchanged (string escapes, TRUNCATE, NOW(),
UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), ADDTIME()). CMake gains ENABLE_MYSQL / ENABLE_SQLITE; MySQL code is behind
WITH_MYSQL so a build can leave MySQL out. PlayerCreationManager's UNION query drops parentheses
SQLite rejects (same result on MySQL).

